- props rest where they should: brazier, man arms folded, man hand on bar, man leaning, man facing, lamp post stand on the pavement or road (within 3 cm).
- rule 3: story props together in the street: brazier, man stooped, man arms folded, man hand on bar, man leaning, man facing stand in front of None and within 0.3 m of each other.
- rule 12: room for phone buttons: Everything to read is left of 0.90 across, and the story props left of 0.95 where the buttons are (brazier 0.56, man stooped 0.63, man arms folded 0.40, man hand on bar 0.68, man leaning 0.81, man facing 0.24).
- rule 5: keep the sky dim: The top third's brightness, left to right: 0.21, 0.23, 0.11 (limit 0.36).
- rule 5: no burnt-out colour: Nothing apart from tiny highlights is at its colour limit.
- main rule: every strong thing points at the same place: where the lines meet 0.63 across, 0.44 down; centre of the brightest parts 0.48 across, 0.36 down; centre of the warm light 0.52 across, 0.39 down; centre of the story props 0.45 across, 0.56 down; centre of brazier 0.49 across, 0.60 down. Together they span 0.18 of the frame wide and 0.24 tall (limit 0.40 x 0.50, holding brazier).

